  "shape_policy": "Nominal: interpolate reference BW parameters in log multiplicity, clamp above M=45 (no measured reference at higher M), then uniformly rescale all pT to the measured O-O K0S mean pT in the same class. Alternative shapes: all seven reference parameter sets, each similarly rescaled, with 0 or 60% soft-pion admixture at T=100 MeV. These are transferred reference fits, NOT measured O-O pion/kaon/proton spectra. The simultaneous reference pion fit excludes pT<0.5 GeV. Resonance decay distortions and the true O-O spectral shapes remain uncertain. In particular the nominal pion mean pT can be too hard: the soft-component scan deliberately permits much softer inclusive spectra. Neither K0S mean pT nor a common BW prescription determines the pion spectrum. The scan is illustrative, not guaranteed coverage.",
  "other_species_policy": {
    "primary_definition": "Count prompt long-lived charged particles and products of short-lived decays. Include Sigma+/-, Xi-/anti-Xi+, Omega-/anti-Omega+. Do not add neutral K0S, K0L, Lambda or their weak-decay daughters; do not separately add strong resonances whose daughters are already in the inclusive primary pi/K/p/hyperon yields.",
    "primary_reference": "https://cds.cern.ch/record/2270008",
    "cms_reference": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.02285",
    "Sigma_ch": "Assumed 0.522455*(p+pbar): direct Boltzmann estimate at T=155 MeV, zero chemical potentials, physical Sigma+/- masses and equal spin degeneracy. 100% normalization width, common across bins. Strong-resonance feed-down not calculated; this is NOT a measured Sigma yield or a strict bound.",
    "Xi_Omega": "Measured charge-summed yields, matched by ordered FT0C class (separate x digitizations agree within 2%). Jacobians from the transferred spectral shapes, not from fitted hyperon spectra. Other-species effect is small.",
    "nuclei": "Assumed 0.005*(p+pbar) at J=1, with 100% common normalization width. A generous tiny-particle allowance, not an O-O measurement. Count particles, not units of charge.",
    "leptons": "Nominal zero. Prompt leptons are explicitly excluded by CMS; ALICE primary charged particles can include prompt leptons. A separate +1% of multiplicity stress test is tabulated below, not assigned a measured uncertainty. Conversion electrons and weak-decay daughters are not primary."
  },
  "uncertainty_policy": "Propagate the stored full joint proxy covariance, plus measured Xi/Omega marginal errors (assumed independent), 100% common Sigma/nuclei nuisance widths and the K0S mean-pT marginal error response (assumed independent bins). No model-discrepancy 5% floor. No fitted closure renormalization. Spectral-shape scan is kept separate. Missing x/cross-species experimental covariances prevent a formal compatibility test.",
  "stats": {
    "conditional_proxy_chi2": 3.2336497132369724,
    "conditional_with_species_assumptions_chi2": 3.2263361050865873,
    "n_points": 8,
    "interpretation": "Conditional Gaussian diagnostics only: no calibrated significance or p-value. Missing multiplicity-axis covariance and true O-O PID spectra; shape scan is not a probability distribution. Stored proxy/anchor errors are analyst assumptions."
  },
